# =========================================================================================
# What is committed, and why.
#
# THE RULE: anything a reviewer needs in order to check a claim is committed. Anything that can be
# regenerated from what is committed is not. The two exceptions to "regenerable means excluded" are
# the replay bundle and one model bundle, because the live demo has to score something and a demo
# that requires a 12-hour training run before it works is not a demo.
# =========================================================================================

# ---- toolchains and caches: never committed ---------------------------------------------
.venv/
.node/
ui/node_modules/
ui/.next/
ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# ---- generated data: excluded, with ONE deliberate exception ----------------------------
# The event stream is ~1.1 GB and the fusion component caches are ~216 MB each. Both regenerate
# from committed configuration, so they stay out.
#
# The EIGHT CURRENT model bundles are the exception — four deployment positions × two personas.
# Committing them means the demo scores on a fresh clone with no training step and no external
# download, and every position the ablation reports can actually be served rather than only cited.
#
# TWO GROUPS ARE DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED, and the distinction is not cosmetic:
#
#   *  `*.prefusion-g1_only` are PRE-REFIT snapshots. They carry the defective fusion weights — the
#      configuration measured at 0.0842 against 0.3515 for the corrected one. A service that loaded
#      one would silently serve scores four times worse than everything we report. They are kept out
#      so that cannot happen by accident.
#   *  `models.backup-*` is a backup of a superseded run, and is excluded by the `data/*` rule below
#      since it sits directly under the data directory.
#
# THE BUNDLES ARE LISTED INDIVIDUALLY, NOT GLOBBED, ON PURPOSE. A pattern like `!data/models/gate-i_*`
# also matches `gate-i_issuer.prefusion-g1_only`, which would pull the defective bundles straight
# back in. Explicitness is the safety property here — if a new position is added, add a line.
#
# NOTE ON THE NEGATION SYNTAX: git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, so
# `data/` is NOT excluded as a directory. Its contents are excluded level by level and the wanted
# paths are re-included at each level. Changing this to a plain `data/` would silently drop every
# model bundle.
data/*
!data/models/
data/models/*
!data/models/gate-i_issuer/
!data/models/gate-i_network/
!data/models/gate-i_acquirer/
!data/models/gate-i_payee_psp/
!data/models/gate-b_issuer/
!data/models/gate-b_network/
!data/models/gate-b_acquirer/
!data/models/gate-b_payee_psp/

# ---- evidence records: COMMITTED ---------------------------------------------------------
# These were previously ignored. They are now committed, for two reasons. They are the artefacts
# that back every number in the deck and the technical document, so a reviewer who cannot read them
# cannot check us. And the read-only screens render by reading them directly from disk, so without
# them a deployed build has nothing to show.
#
# Rendered report bodies stay out — they are formatted views over the JSON, not new evidence.
reports/*.html
reports/figures/
reports/_tmp_*.json

# ---- committed deliberately ------------------------------------------------------------
# bundles/     the offline replay bundle the demo path reads
# attack/cache/  the composed-attack cache, part of the reproducible run
# grammar/ config/ docs/  the specification the whole system is generated from
!bundles/
